"I work in November.","example_es":"(noviembre)","difficulty":1,"tags":["months"]},{"id":"en-december","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"December","translation_es":"diciembre","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/dɪˈsɛmbər/","romanization":null,"emoji":"📅","example_en":"We go home in December.","example_es":"(diciembre)","difficulty":1,"tags":["months"]},{"id":"en-first","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"first","translation_es":"primero / primera","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/fɜrst/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"May first","example_es":"el primero de mayo","difficulty":1,"tags":["ordinals"]},{"id":"en-second","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"second","translation_es":"segundo / segunda","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈsɛkənd/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"June second","example_es":"el 2 de junio","difficulty":1,"tags":["ordinals"]},{"id":"en-third","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"third","translation_es":"tercero / tercera","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/θɜrd/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"March third","example_es":"el 3 de marzo","difficulty":1,"tags":["ordinals"]},{"id":"en-fourth","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"fourth","translation_es":"cuarto / cuarta","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/fɔrθ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"July fourth","example_es":"el 4 de julio","difficulty":1,"tags":["ordinals"]},{"id":"en-fifth","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u09","text":"fifth","translation_es":"quinto / quinta","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/fɪfθ/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"April fifth","example_es":"el 5 de abril","difficulty":1,"tags":["ordinals"]},{"id":"en-me","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u11","text":"me","translation_es":"me / a mí","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/mi/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Can you help me?","example_es":"¿Me podés ayudar?","difficulty":1,"tags":["pronouns"]},{"id":"en-them","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u11","text":"them","translation_es":"los / las (a ellos, a ellas)","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ðɛm/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"I love them.","example_es":"Me encantan. / Los quiero.","difficulty":1,"tags":["pronouns"]},{"id":"en-postcard","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u12","text":"postcard","translation_es":"postal","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈpoʊstˌkɑrd/","romanization":null,"emoji":"🏞️","example_en":"I have a postcard from Ana.","example_es":"Tengo una postal de Ana.","difficulty":1,"tags":["messages"]},{"id":"en-see-you","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u12","text":"see you","translation_es":"nos vemos","accepted_translations":[],"ipa":"/ˈsi ju/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"See you on Monday!","example_es":"¡Nos vemos el lunes!","difficulty":1,"tags":["messages","greetings"]},{"id":"en-back-at","language_code":"en","unit_id":"a1-u12","text":"back at","translation_es":"vuelvo a las / de vuelta a las","accepted_translations":["vuelvo a las","de vuelta a las"],"ipa":"/bæk æt/","romanization":null,"emoji":null,"example_en":"Back at five.","example_es":"Vuelvo a las cinco.","difficulty":1,"tags":["messages"]}],"lessons":[{"id":"a1-u01-l01","unit_id":"a1-u01","position":1,"title_es":"Hola y chau","objective_es":"Saludar y despedirte; decir sí y no.","intro":{"explanation":"Hello y hi son «hola»; hi es más informal. Para despedirte: goodbye o, más informal, bye.","examples":[{"target":"Hello, Ana!","base":"¡Hola, Ana!"},{"target":"Bye, Mom!","base":"¡Chau, mamá!"},{"target":"No, thank you.","base":"No, gracias."}]},"takeaways":["Saludás con hello o hi.","Te despedís con goodbye o bye.","Decís yes y no."]},{"id":"a1-u01-l02","unit_id":"a1-u01","position":2,"title_es":"Momentos del día","objective_es":"Saludar según la hora del día.","intro":{"explanation":"Good morning es para la mañana, good afternoon para la tarde y good evening para saludar a la noche. Good night es sólo para despedirte o irte a dormir.","examples":[{"target":"Good morning, everyone!","base":"¡Buenos días a todos!"},{"target":"Good evening! Welcome.","base":"¡Buenas noches! Bienvenidos."},{"target":"Good night! See you tomorrow.","base":"¡Buenas noches! Hasta mañana."}]},"takeaways":["Saludás con good morning, good afternoon o good evening según la hora.","Usás good night sólo para despedirte."]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04","unit_id":"a1-u02","position":5,"title_es":"He is, she is","objective_es":"Hablar de otras personas con is.","intro":{"explanation":"Con he, she e it el verbo es is: he is, she is, it is. Al hablar se contrae: he’s, she’s.","examples":[{"target":"He is a teacher.","base":"Él es profesor."},{"target":"She's my friend.","base":"Ella es mi amiga."}]},"takeaways":["Usás is con he, she e it.","Presentás a otra persona con he is o she is."]},{"id":"a1-u02-l05","unit_id":"a1-u02","position":7,"title_es":"Negar y preguntar","objective_es":"Formar oraciones negativas y preguntas con to be.","intro":{"explanation":"Para negar, not va después de to be: I am not, she is not (isn’t). Para preguntar, el verbo va primero: Are you tired?","examples":[{"target":"I'm not tired.","base":"No estoy cansado."},{"target":"Is she a student?","base":"¿Ella es estudiante?"}]},"takeaways":["Negás con not después de am, is o are.","Preguntás poniendo el verbo primero: Are you…?"]},{"id":"a1-u03-l03","unit_id":"a1-u03","position":4,"title_es":"Hasta veinte","objective_es":"Usar números más grandes: 11, 12, 15 y 20.","intro":{"explanation":"Eleven y twelve son especiales. Del 13 al 19 terminan en -teen: fifteen. Twenty es veinte. Ojo: fifteen (15) y fifty (50) suenan parecido.","examples":[{"target":"I have twelve friends.","base":"Tengo doce amigos."},{"target":"Fifteen dollars.","base":"Quince dólares."}]},"takeaways":["Decís 11, 12, 15 y 20.","Reconocés la terminación -teen."]},{"id":"a1-u04-l04","unit_id":"a1-u04","position":5,"title_es":"Su, nuestro y su de ellos","objective_es":"Usar his, her, our y their.","intro":{"explanation":"En inglés «su» cambia según el dueño: his (de él), her (de ella), their (de ellos). Our es «nuestro» o «nuestra».","examples":[{"target":"His name is Tom.","base":"Su nombre (de él) es Tom."},{"target":"Our mother is a teacher.","base":"Nuestra madre es profesora."}]},"takeaways":["Elegís his o her según quién es el dueño.","Usás our y their."]},{"id":"a1-u05-l02","unit_id":"a1-u05","position":2,"title_es":"A o an","objective_es":"Elegir a o an según el sonido de la palabra.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u05-l06","unit_id":"a1-u05","position":12,"title_es":"Uno, dos, muchos","objective_es":"Formar plurales regulares e irregulares frecuentes.","intro":{"explanation":"Casi siempre el plural se forma con -s: one book, two books. Algunas palabras muy usadas cambian: man → men, woman → women. Children (niños) y people (personas) ya son plurales.","examples":[{"target":"one pen, three pens","base":"una lapicera, tres lapiceras"},{"target":"These women are teachers.","base":"Estas mujeres son profesoras."}]},"takeaways":["Formás el plural con -s: books, keys.","Usás men, women, children y people."]},{"id":"a1-u06-l04","unit_id":"a1-u06","position":5,"title_es":"Hay una cama","objective_es":"Usar there is y there are.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u06-l05","unit_id":"a1-u06","position":7,"title_es":"¿Dónde está?","objective_es":"Ubicar cosas con in, on, under y next to.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u07-l04","unit_id":"a1-u07","position":5,"title_es":"Quiero un café","objective_es":"Pedir lo que querés con want y please.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u08-l02","unit_id":"a1-u08","position":2,"title_es":"Lo que hago","objective_es":"Trabajar, estudiar, leer, jugar, mirar, dormir y vivir.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u08-l04","unit_id":"a1-u08","position":5,"title_es":"No tomo café","objective_es":"Negar con don't y doesn't.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u09-l03","unit_id":"a1-u09","position":4,"title_es":"Hoy, mañana y las partes del día","objective_es":"Today, tomorrow, morning, afternoon y evening.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u09-l04","unit_id":"a1-u09","position":5,"title_es":"¿Qué hora es?","objective_es":"Decir la hora con o'clock y half past.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u09-l06","unit_id":"a1-u09","position":12,"title_es":"Meses y fechas","objective_es":"Decir los meses y las fechas, y preguntar cuándo es algo.","intro":{"explanation":"Los meses se escriben con mayúscula. Con el mes solo se usa in (in May); con la fecha, on (on May third). En la fecha se dice el número ordinal: first, second, third, fourth, fifth… (del 4 en adelante, casi siempre -th).","examples":[{"target":"My birthday is in May.","base":"Mi cumpleaños es en mayo."},{"target":"It is on May third.","base":"Es el 3 de mayo."}]},"takeaways":["Decís los doce meses.","Usás in con el mes y on con la fecha.","Decís una fecha con first, second, third…"]},{"id":"a1-u10-l02","unit_id":"a1-u10","position":2,"title_es":"Lugares para ir","objective_es":"Restaurante, supermercado, negocio, museo, cine y biblioteca.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u10-l05","unit_id":"a1-u10","position":7,"title_es":"Doblá a la izquierda","objective_es":"Dar indicaciones: left, right, turn y straight on.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u11-l02","unit_id":"a1-u11","position":2,"title_es":"Me encanta, lo odio","objective_es":"Love, hate y don’t like.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u11-l03","unit_id":"a1-u11","position":4,"title_es":"Pasatiempos","objective_es":"Bailar, cantar, nadar, cocinar y viajar.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u12-l03","unit_id":"a1-u12","position":4,"title_es":"En clase","objective_es":"Pedir ayuda: repetir, hablar despacio y no entender.","intro":null,"takeaways":[]},{"id":"a1-u12-l06","unit_id":"a1-u12","position":12,"title_es":"Mensajes y postales","objective_es":"Leer y escribir mensajes muy breves, notas y postales.","intro":{"explanation":"Un mensaje o una nota va al grano: dónde estás y cuándo volvés («Back at five»). Una postal saluda, cuenta algo y se despide («See you on Sunday! Love, Ana»).","examples":[{"target":"I am at the bank. Back at four.","base":"Estoy en el banco. Vuelvo a las cuatro."},{"target":"See you on Sunday!","base":"¡Nos vemos el domingo!"}]},"takeaways":["Entendés notas, mensajes y postales breves.","Escribís una nota del tipo «Back at five»."]},{"id":"a1-u14-l01","unit_id":"a1-u14","position":1,"title_es":"Del 21 al 100","objective_es":"Contar de diez en diez hasta cien y armar los números del 21 al 99.","intro":{"explanation":"Las decenas terminan en -ty: thirty (30), forty (40), fifty (50). Forty se escribe sin u, aunque four la lleva. Del 21 al 99 se unen con guion: twenty-one, thirty-five. El 100 es one hundred.","examples":[{"target":"Thirty-five students.","base":"Treinta y cinco estudiantes."},{"target":"My grandmother is ninety.","base":"Mi abuela tiene noventa años."}]},"takeaways":["Contás de diez en diez hasta one hundred.","Armás los números del 21 al 99 con guion: forty-two."]}],"exercises":[{"id":"a1-u01-l01-e11","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l01","position":11,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___, Ana!","translation":"Situación: llegás a clase y ves a tu amiga Ana. ¿Qué le decís?","options":["Hello","Goodbye","Thank you","You're welcome"]},"answer":"Hello","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Al llegar se saluda: Hello (o Hi). Goodbye es para irse.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-hello"]},{"id":"a1-u01-l01-e12","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l01","position":12,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___, Tom!","translation":"Situación: te vas de la casa de Tom. ¿Qué le decís?","options":["Bye","Hello","Sorry","Please"]},"answer":"Bye","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Al irse se dice Bye o Goodbye.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-bye"]},{"id":"a1-u01-l01-e13","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l01","position":13,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y respondé","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"en.stim.a1-u01-lm-goodbye","setting":"Tom sale de la clase.","speakers":[{"name":"Tom","voice":"a"}],"rate":0.85,"lines":[{"speaker":"Tom","text":"Goodbye!"}]},"question":"¿Qué significa lo que dice Tom?","options":["Chau","Hola","Gracias","Perdón"]},"answer":"Chau","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Tom dice «Goodbye!»: es una despedida (chau).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":[]},{"id":"a1-u01-l02-e11","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l02","position":11,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___, Ana!","translation":"Situación: son las 9 de la mañana y entrás a la oficina. ¿Cómo saludás a Ana?","options":["Good morning","Good night","Good evening","Goodbye"]},"answer":"Good morning","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"A la mañana: Good morning. Good night es para despedirse a la noche.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-good-morning"]},{"id":"a1-u01-l02-e12","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l02","position":12,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completá la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___, Tom!","translation":"Situación: son las 11 de la noche y te vas a dormir. ¿Qué le decís a Tom?","options":["Good night","Good morning","Good afternoon","Hello"]},"answer":"Good night","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Good night se usa para despedirse a la noche o antes de dormir.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-good-night"]},{"id":"a1-u01-l02-e13","lesson_id":"a1-u01-l02","position":13,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"🌙 😴","translation":"Situación: es de noche y te vas a dormir. Escribí en inglés qué le decís a tu familia."},"answer":"Good night.","accepted_answers":["Goodnight.","Good night, everyone."],"explanation_es":"Antes de dormir se dice Good night (no Good evening, que es un saludo).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-good-night"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04-e11","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l04","position":11,"type":"image_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué muestra la imagen?","payload":{"type":"image_choice","emoji":"🧑‍⚕️","options":["doctor","teacher","student","friend"]},"answer":"doctor","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-doctor"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04-e12","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l04","position":12,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"doctor","right":"médico / médica"},{"left":"nurse","right":"enfermero / enfermera"},{"left":"engineer","right":"ingeniero / ingeniera"},{"left":"waiter","right":"mozo / moza"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-doctor","en-nurse","en-engineer","en-waiter"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04-e13","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l04","position":13,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"She is a nurse.","options":["She is a nurse.","She is a teacher.","He is a nurse.","She is a doctor."]},"answer":"She is a nurse.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["en-nurse","en-doctor","en-she","en-is"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04-e14","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l04","position":14,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «engineer»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"engineer","options":["ingeniero / ingeniera","médico / médica","mozo / moza","profesor / profesora"]},"answer":"ingeniero / ingeniera","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-engineer"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l04-e15","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l04","position":15,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"👨‍🏫","translation":"Escribí en inglés qué es este hombre. Empezá con He."},"answer":"He is a teacher.","accepted_answers":["He's a teacher."],"explanation_es":"Profesión con to be y a: He is a teacher.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-he","en-is","en-teacher"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l05-e11","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l05","position":11,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"I am tired.","translation":"Escribí la oración en negativa."},"answer":"I am not tired.","accepted_answers":["I'm not tired."],"explanation_es":"Negativa: am + not → I am not (I’m not) tired.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-am","en-not","en-tired"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l05-e12","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l05","position":12,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"She is a teacher.","translation":"Escribí la oración como pregunta."},"answer":"Is she a teacher?","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Pregunta con to be: el verbo va primero. Is she…?","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-is","en-she","en-teacher"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l05-e13","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l05","position":13,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"They are students.","translation":"Escribí la oración en negativa."},"answer":"They are not students.","accepted_answers":["They aren't students.","They're not students."],"explanation_es":"They are not = they aren’t = they’re not.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-are","en-not","en-student"]},{"id":"a1-u02-l05-e14","lesson_id":"a1-u02-l05","position":14,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Respondé en inglés","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"You are happy.","translation":"Escribí la oración como pregunta."},"answer":"Are you happy?","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Are va antes de you en la pregunta: Are you happy?","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-are","en-you","en-happy"]},{"id":"a1-u03-l03-e10","lesson_id":"a1-u03-l03","position":10,"type":"image_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué muestra la imagen?","payload":{"type":"image_choice","emoji":"0️⃣","options":["zero","ten","one","two"]},"answer":"zero","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-zero"]},{"id":"a1-u03-l03-e11","lesson_id":"a1-u03-l03","position":11,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"¿Qué significa «thirteen»?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"thirteen","options":["trece","tres","catorce","dieciséis"]},"answer":"trece","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["en-thirteen"]},{"id":"a1-u03-l03-e12","lesson_id":"a1-u03-l03","position":12,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Uní cada palabra con su significado","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"fourteen","right":"catorce"},{"left":"sixteen","right":"dieciséis"},{"left":"eighteen","right":"dieciocho"},{"left":"nineteen","right":"diecinueve"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["en-fourteen","en-sixteen","en-eighteen","en-nineteen"]},{"id":"a1-u03-l03-e13","lesson_id":"a1-u03-l03","position":13,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Escuchá y elegí lo que oís","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"